{"name":"Wood Stain Brown","hex":"#796a4e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wood","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The substance making up the central part of the trunk and branches of a tree. Used as a material for construction, to manufacture various items, etc. or as fuel.","The wood from a particular species of tree."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or plant with trees.","To hide behind trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wood"},{"term":"stain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A discolored spot or area caused by spillage or other contact with certain fluids or substances.","A blemish on one's character or reputation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To discolor, as by spilling or other contact with a fluid or substance.","To taint or tarnish someone's character or reputation"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stain"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wood stain","blocks":[{"text":"Wood stain is used in woodworking, construction, and architectural finishing to modify the color and appearance of wood while allowing the grain pattern to remain visible. Unlike paint, which forms an opaque surface coating, stains are typically formulated to penetrate wood fibers or lightly coat the surface, enhancing natural texture rather than concealing it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f9/Woodstainer.JPG/330px-Woodstainer.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood_stain","wikidata":"Q16060211"},{"title":"Wood","blocks":[{"text":"Wood is a natural, lignocellulosic material derived primarily from the secondary xylem of trees and other woody plants, where it provides mechanical support and in the functional sapwood, conducts water and dissolved minerals. Being a natural material, it is characterized as an organic material – a natural composite of cellulosic fibers that are strong in tension and embedded in a matrix of lignin and hemicelluloses that resists compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/16_wood_samples.jpg/330px-16_wood_samples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood","wikidata":"Q287"},{"title":"Stain","blocks":[{"text":"A stain is a discoloration that can be clearly distinguished from the surface, material, or medium it is found upon. They are caused by the chemical or physical interaction of two dissimilar materials. Accidental staining may make materials appear used, degraded or permanently unclean. Intentional staining is used in biochemical research, and for artistic effect, such as in wood staining, rust staining and stained glass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Patternspage.jpg/330px-Patternspage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stain","wikidata":"Q2733470"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Lasure_bleue.JPG/500px-Lasure_bleue.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont